{
  // LOOM BRAIN W10 — the CLI build (#3936).
  //
  // The scheduled scan runs OUTSIDE the console image: it is a plain Node
  // process launched by `.github/workflows/loom-brain-scan.yml`, because the
  // console Container App is itself one of the things that may be STOPPED when
  // the estate is paused. A scheduler that could only run inside the thing it
  // monitors cannot report that the thing is down.
  //
  // ── WHY THERE IS NO `paths` MAPPING HERE, DELIBERATELY ────────────────────
  // The console's tsconfig maps `@/*`. `tsc` RESOLVES that mapping for
  // typechecking but does NOT rewrite the specifier on emit, so a compiled
  // `require('@/lib/x')` fails at runtime with a module-not-found that looks
  // like a broken install. Omitting `paths` makes an alias import a COMPILE
  // error in this config instead — the failure lands at build time, in CI, with
  // the offending file named, rather than at 04:11 UTC in a scheduled run.
  //
  // Everything the CLI reaches (`lib/brain/**`, `lib/estate/pause-state`,
  // `lib/azure/cloud-endpoints` + `cloud-boundary` + `cloud-endpoints-graph`,
  // `app/api/admin/brain/_lib/wire-bindings`) is alias-free by construction and
  // `../__tests__/cli-buildable.test.ts` asserts that so the property cannot
  // rot silently.
  //
  // ── COMMONJS ON PURPOSE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // `apps/fiab-console/package.json` has no `"type": "module"`, so emitted `.js`
  // is CJS and Node resolves the extensionless relative imports the source uses.
  // An ESM emit would need every specifier rewritten with a `.js` suffix.
  //
  // Strictness matches the console's own tsconfig: `strict: true` is not
  // optional here, because `lib/brain/types.ts` and `lib/estate/pause-state.ts`
  // carry build-checked type assertions that only hold under strict mode.
  //
  // ── WHY outDir SITS UNDER apps/fiab-console AND NOT AT THE REPO ROOT ──────
  // Node resolves `@azure/cosmos` and `@azure/identity` by walking UP from the
  // emitted file. The console is a standalone pnpm package, so those live in
  // `apps/fiab-console/node_modules` and NOT at the repo root. Emitting to
  // `<repo>/temp` produced `Cannot find module '@azure/cosmos'` on the first
  // smoke run — measured, not theorised. `apps/fiab-console/temp/**` is covered
  // by the root `.gitignore` `temp/` rule and by this project's own
  // `tsconfig.build.json` exclude list.
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "lib": ["ES2022"],
    "module": "commonjs",
    "moduleResolution": "node10",
    "strict": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "sourceMap": true,
    "noEmit": false,
    "declaration": false,
    "rootDir": "../../..",
    "outDir": "../../../temp/brain-scan-build"
  },
  // ── `include`, NOT `files` — THIS SHIPPED WRONG (review of #4014) ─────────
  //
  // `files: ["./cli.ts"]` makes tsc's emit closure follow STATIC imports only.
  // Both history specifiers are assembled at RUNTIME precisely so tsc cannot
  // resolve them while #3935 is unmerged — so the history module was never
  // emitted at all. Measured: 34 emitted .js files, none under
  // `lib/brain/history/`. The OK path would have failed at 04:11 UTC with a
  // module-not-found, before AND after #3935 lands, and no gate could see it.
  //
  // `include` fixes it and is self-healing: the glob below matches zero files
  // today (W9 is not on this branch) and picks up `lib/brain/history/**` the
  // moment it lands, with no second edit. A config whose globs match zero files
  // in TOTAL is an error, but `./cli.ts` always matches, so the history glob
  // being empty is fine.
  //
  // `__tests__/history-wiring.test.ts` asserts this include covers the history
  // directory, and resolves both runtime specifiers against a stub tree — so
  // neither half of that defect can return silently.
  "include": ["./cli.ts", "../history/**/*.ts"],
  "exclude": ["**/__tests__/**", "**/*.test.ts"]
}
